{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And they kept the children alive.</b> They supplied them with water and food. The first Targum renders וְקַיָּמָא, and the second וְקַיֵּמְתֻן — because in Hebrew, for many females, this word [וַתְּחַיֵּיןָ] and others like it serve both as פָּעַל (causative) and as פְּעַלְתֶּם (simple active), e.g. ״וַתֹּאמַרְנָה אִישׁ מִצְרִי״ (Exodus 2) — past tense, as וַיֹּאמְרוּ for males; ״וַתְּדַבֵּרְנָה בְּפִיכֶם״ (Jeremiah 44) — meaning דִּבַּרְתֶּן, as וַתְּדַבְּרוּ for males; and likewise ״וַתְּחַלְּלֶנָה אֹתִי אֶל עַמִּי״ (Ezekiel 13) — past tense, meaning חִלַּלְתֶּן, as וַתְּחַלְּלוּ for males."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:09.437843148Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}